    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE GREAT LAKES WAVE HEIGHT</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Wave height (feet, one continuous gradient): <b>0</b> dark blue → <b>2</b> blue/cyan → <b>5</b> cyan/green → <b>9</b> green/yellow → <b>12–15</b> yellow-orange → orange → <b>20</b> red → <b>23–26</b> red-violet → violet → <b>30+</b> dark purple extreme. Model maximum this run: <b>3.1 ft</b>. Values above 30 ft stay dark purple. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 09:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260926-0100Z<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of temperature and ice layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
